WEBVTT

NOTE Actual full-workspace tutorial recording. Prepared starter QA account; five later phases explicitly opened. No earned passes, AI, execution, edits or submissions. Normal speed; no added holds.

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.920
1 of 6. Start with the UML model
Open UML model to inspect and edit the model’s fields and operations. Use the accepted requirements and phase brief to decide what the model must represent.

2
00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:12.880
2 of 6. Define the API contracts
Open API contracts. Record each operation’s inputs, outputs and error cases, and finish any open contract form before leaving it.

3
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.880
3 of 6. Trace a sequence
Open Sequence diagram to describe how the parts interact. Check that the messages match your contracts and model.

4
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.760
4 of 6. Explain your design decisions
Use Decisions to record why you chose this design and what tradeoffs it makes. Keep the explanation consistent with the model and contracts.

5
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:30.760
5 of 6. Review the design as a whole
Open Review to inspect inconsistencies, check the saved design, then choose Submit for review. Use the returned evidence to revise any gaps before trying again.

6
00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:37.680
6 of 6. Return whenever you need help
Replay tutorial brings these steps back. Optional phase guide opens the lessons. In the workspace mentor, Guided offers hints. Agentic proposes changes: compare them, explain this exact version in your own words, then choose Apply only if your explanation is accepted. A changed proposal needs a new explanation.
